{"id": "ffdec8850c", "title": "Show the first mate's closing words above the message box", "goal": "Build a task's approved plan with the captain's submitted answers. The first mate's closing words of each turn become its line above the message box, with today's typed line as the fallback. They are kept to about 40 characters by instruction alone, and say what took effect this turn, never the answer. Emote words are dropped, because the emote is motion only. The closing words also show in the card's reply thread, kept to one sentence there.", "userWords": "Another user experience question I want fable crewmate to look at. It's with the little chat messages that we show right above the main chat input. Right now, I think we have some rules on what will show up and how it will fade. I'm wondering whether we should actually lean on the firstmate agent's text response, the final text response in each turn to be the message that we show as the agent response. That will make everything more consistent with how the model is trained. And I think we should restrict the final text response to a certain length so that it doesn't end up being too long. And that should be done by instruction only. Have the crewmates look into this idea and assess whether we can indeed drive an improvement through that. The goal is that every user ask will end up seeing a response that explains what firstmate actually did. So the user is very clear on what's happening.", "parentTitle": "Show the first mate's final words as its reply to every ask", "way": "plan-piece", "month": "2026-10", "tags": ["feature", "prompts"]}
